	(lib_symbols)
	(text_box "LAYOUT NOTE: GENERAL PCB LAYOUT\n1. Stack-up: 4 layers. L1 parts + power, L2 solid GND (no splits), L3 power pours (VBUS, +5V, +3V3), L4 signals. 2 oz outer copper for the bridge.\n2. One GND net. Keep the bridge return (J1/J2, bulk caps, shunts) in its own area of the plane and join logic GND to it near U4/the shunts, not across the bridge current path.\n3. VBUS, PHASE_x and shunt GND: short, wide pours on several layers, many vias, no necking.\n4. Switch nodes (VM_SW, 5V_SW, 3V3_SW, PHASE_x): minimal copper; no analog traces next to or under them.\n5. ISENSE, VSENSE, VBUS_SENSE, NTC: route away from SW/phase copper; RC caps at the MCU pins.\n6. EtherCAT pairs 100 ohm diff; T1/T2 isolation gap kept clear.\n7. Mark XT30 polarity on silk (+ = pad 2 in the KiCad footprint); check against the part before ordering.\n8. Add test pads: SWD, UART, +VM, +5V, +3V3, +3V3A, ISENSE_A/B/C, GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
